{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>אספרם</b> — How can I count them when they are more than the sand, if I were always awake? For half of a person's life he is asleep — yet I am still with you. That is, I will be with you always and not die. I cannot count them, and behold: I have awakened, and there is no mention of sleep there, similar to: אשבעה בהקיץ תמונתך. And another interpretation: I in righteousness behold Your face, in מראות אלהים at night; therefore: אשבעה בהקיץ from the form of divine visions. And מראות אלהים goes two ways, and your re'a (friend/companion) — when I think in my heart to know your re'a, and behold it is like a divine vision, and the body lies sleeping while the human soul cleaves to the supernal soul, then you see wondrous forms; therefore: I have awakened and I am still with you, for this is not like all other dreams."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 139, :notes {0 "The comment weaves together interpretations of three adjacent verses (Ps. 17:15 אשביעה בהקיץ תמונתך; Num. 12:6 במראה אלהים; and the verse under comment). The re'a/re'ak thread is textually dense and possibly corrupt; rendered hyper-literally as it stands."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:42:16.619236701Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}